Package: SamplingCoordination
Type: Package
Title: Coordination of Samples for Complex Rotative Designs
Version: 1.0.2
Author: José Zea <jfzeac@unal.edu.co>,
    Hugo Andres Gutierrez Rojas <andres.gutierrez@cepal.org>,
    Stalyn Guerrero <syguerrerog@unal.edu.co>,
    Yury Vanessa Ochoa Montes <yury.ochoa@urosario.edu.co>
Maintainer: Hugo Andres Gutierrez Rojas <andres.gutierrez@cepal.org>
Description: Provides tools for the coordination and management of samples
    in complex rotative survey designs. Implements permanent, colocated,
    sequential Poisson and Pareto random numbers, rotating panel schemes
    (4-0-0, 5-0-0 and 2-2-2), allocation of primary sampling units (PSU) to
    mini-panels by socioeconomic stratum with iterative proportional fitting,
    overlap control between successive periods, and negative or positive
    coordination of a new sample with previous samples. Designed for use in
    household and social surveys that require controlled sample renewal
    across periods.
License: GPL (>= 2)
Encoding: UTF-8
